# ONNX inference in Resolve Studio 21.2.0.5: what describe() sets, 2026-11-27.
#
# Backlog row 19. The question: the host answered `describe failed on plugin
# com.ofxplugindeveloper.onnxinference, error code 4` and never instantiated the
# plug-in, so every frame it produced was the source. Which of the writes in
# describe() does it refuse, and does the effect render once the refusal is out
# of the way?

## 1. Why a probe, and what it reports

`OFX::Log` writes nothing in a release build, and a refused describe and a
working one produce the same pixels until an instance exists. So the measurement
is a probe in a scratch copy of the template (`.validation/onnx-probe/`, built
against `.ofx-ref`, never committed): every describe() step appends one line to
the file named in `$OFXCL_PROBE`, and the three property writes that can throw
report what the host answered instead of aborting describe - so one host session
lists all of them:

    describe begin
    describe flags=ok
    describe cpu_property=ok | failed reason=<what()> | failed status=<n>
    describe nosa_property=...
    describe cuda_render=...
    describe end

`describe begin` / `flags=ok` / `end` bracket the plain setters (labels, grouping,
description, both contexts, bit depth, single instance, frame threading,
multi-resolution, tiles, temporal clip access, render-twice, multiple-PARs,
multiple-depths, render-thread-safety), which throw nothing and therefore need no
line of their own.

## 2. What the host accepts  [V]

One run of the probe bundle through `tests/resolve/poc.py` (model shipped as
`Contents/Resources/model.onnx`), OFX log of that session:

    describe begin
    describe flags=ok
    describe cpu_property=failed reason=OfxImageEffectPropCPURenderSupported
    describe nosa_property=ok
    describe cuda_render=ok
    describe end

Read: Resolve 21.2.0.5 accepts every write the template makes in describe() -
labels, grouping, description, `eContextFilter` and `eContextGeneral`, float bit
depth, `setSingleInstance(false)`, `setHostFrameThreading(false)`,
`setSupportsMultiResolution(false)`, `setSupportsTiles(false)`,
`setTemporalClipAccess(false)`, `setRenderTwiceAlways(false)`,
`setSupportsMultipleClipPARs(false)`, `setSupportsMultipleClipDepths(false)`,
`setRenderThreadSafety(eRenderInstanceSafe)`,
`kOfxImageEffectPropNoSpatialAwareness` and `setSupportsCudaRender(false)` - and
rejects exactly one: `kOfxImageEffectPropCPURenderSupported`.

The reason string is the support library's `PropertyUnknownToHost`, whose
`what()` is the property name (`Support/Library/ofxsProperty.cpp:8-40`: an
unknown property status becomes that exception; it is not a `Suite` exception, so
no status number is carried).

## 3. Where "error code 4" comes from  [I]

`Support/Library/ofxsImageEffect.cpp`, the main-entry dispatcher, catches in
this order: `OFX::Exception::Suite` -> `stat = ex.status()` (:2831-2838);
`HostInadequate` -> `kOfxStatErrMissingHostFeature` (:2849-2851);
`PropertyUnknownToHost` -> `kOfxStatErrMissingHostFeature` (:2859-2861). So a
describe() that lets `PropertyUnknownToHost` escape returns status 4, and 4 is
`kOfxStatErrMissingHostFeature` (`include/ofxCore.h:916`) - the number Resolve
prints after `describe failed on plugin ...`.

## 4. The same describe(), one write apart  [V]

At the session that produced the message (2026-11-26 22:21, commit 764547a) the
source wrote all three properties unguarded
(`templates/onnx-inference-ofx/src/Plugin.cpp:418/419/423`); the host logged
`describe failed ... error code 4` once, then `Plugin [...] is not available`
2240 times and rendered the source (`mae 0.0`, `resolve-project-route.log` §6).

On 2026-11-27 the only change is a `try`/`catch` around the
`kOfxImageEffectPropCPURenderSupported` write (commit be06bc4). With it the same
host loads the bundle, creates the filter context and renders 1920x1080:

    validate  pass  1 .ofx, decoders ['ffmpeg']
    install   pass  C:\Program Files\Common Files\OFX\Plugins\OnnxInference.ofx.bundle
    connect   pass  DaVinci Resolve Studio 21.2.0.5
    gpu       pass  Selected compute API: CUDA
    build     pass  poc: ONNX Inference on source.png
    render    pass  poc00108000.png
    check     pass  1920x1080 via ffmpeg
    quit      pass  API quit, then the recorded PID
    report: tests/resolve/reports/poc-2026-11-27T16-21-43+00-00.json

Committed as `resolve-onnx-host-report.json` beside this file. The host's own
log for the session carries `OFX: loading com.ofxplugindeveloper.onnxinference`
and no `describe failed` line.

## 5. The frame is the model's output, not a copy  [V]

Bundle: the template's own, built with `ONNXRUNTIME_ROOT=.validation/ort-1.32.0`
(the CPU package - no execution provider beside the .ofx), model
`templates/onnx-inference-ofx/models/test_conv.onnx` copied to
`Contents/Resources/model.onnx`.

    frame vs source          mae 94.872843, max_pixel 255, 8294400 bytes
    frame vs the model run   0..1 input:  mae 0.198, max 0.5 (of 255),
      on the CPU                            correlation 0.9994
    frame vs the model run   0..255 input: mae 2.142, max 8, correlation 0.9135

The CPU reference is `onnxruntime` 1.23.2 in this repository's venv, the same
PNG decoded to RGB, packed planar `[1,3,H,W]`, the model's single `Conv` run on
`CPUExecutionProvider`, output clipped to 0..255. Matching the host frame to
within half an 8-bit level at input scale 0..1 says two things at once: the host
hands the plug-in pixels in 0..1, and the frame it recorded is that convolution,
not the source (which differs by 94.9 levels).

## 6. What stays unmeasured

- The CUDA execution provider inside Resolve: this run shipped the CPU package,
  so the provider path of row 19 is still only measured up to "the bundle loads".
- The project round trip (`ImportProject` + `LoadProject`) has not been
  re-rendered since the guard; the render above is `poc.py`'s direct route.
- Tiles, proxy and colour management: the model still sees whatever the host
  hands over, in 0..1, with no colourspace read.
